{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 37, :comments ["<b>And Yitzchak answered.</b> Behold, he still had the wherewithal to bless him, but because he recognized him and knew that he was worthy of curse and an enemy to Yaakov, he was careful about blessing him, since that would be the opposite of what he had just said to Yaakov — ״אֹרְרֶיךָ אָרוּר.״ Therefore he made excuses to Esav and withheld a blessing from him. And for this reason Scripture doubled the expression ״וַיַּעַן וַיֹּאמֶר לְעֵשָׂו״ — meaning that this answer was merely a thing said, and not the true sentiment in Yitzchak's heart."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:44:00.089962513Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}